Overview

The Silent Auction Program is a Python-based console application that allows multiple participants to place their bids secretly.
After all participants have entered their bids, the program determines and displays the winner — the person who placed the highest bid.

Features

✅ Accepts multiple bidders and their bid amounts
✅ Clears the screen between bidders (for privacy)
✅ Automatically determines the highest bidder
✅ Displays the winner with their bid amount
✅ Beginner-friendly, with simple logic and clean structure

Concepts Used

The program asks each participant for their name and bid amount.
After entering a bid, the user specifies if there are more bidders.
If yes, the screen is cleared, and the next bidder enters their bid.
When no more bidders remain, the program finds the highest bid and announces the winner.

        
